## 🎓 PART 7: How to Interpret the Output

### What the KPIs Mean

| KPI | Meaning | Good Value |
|-----|---------|------------|
| Total Revenue | Sum of all sales | High |
| Total Profit | Sum of all profit | High |
| Profit Margin | Profit / Revenue × 100 | > 10% |
| Total Orders | Count of unique orders | High |
| Avg Order Value | Revenue / Orders | Depends |
| Avg Discount | Mean discount % | < 20% |

### What the Charts Tell You

**Region-wise bar chart:**
- Tall bar = high sales
- Red bar = loss-making region → needs investigation

**Discount vs Profit scatter:**
- Downward trend = discount kills profit
- Points below zero = loss-making orders

**Monthly trend:**
- Peak month = best month for sales
- Dip = low season

**Profit status pie:**
- Green slice = profitable orders
- Red slice = loss-making orders → needs fixing

